From 43473a5df6465ea635f010fe6d3cf4737d9b30e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:53:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] rdna-boosts: block 13: MTP draft vocabulary subset
 (--spec-draft-mtp-vocab N)

The MTP draft head scores only the LM-head rows for token ids < N plus every
control/user-defined id, then scatters the logits into a full-vocabulary row
of -inf: the speculator still sees a full-vocab logit row and the target's
verification is untouched, so the trim can only lose proposals, never change
an accepted token.  Opt-in and default off (-spec-draft-mtp-vocab 0 builds no
subset and adds no graph node).

Contents:
- common: --spec-draft-mtp-vocab N + LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_DRAFT_MTP_VOCAB, plumbed
  to llama_context_params::mtp_draft_vocab for the MTP draft context only.
- src: llama_mtp_draft_vocab (verbatim LM-head row copy in its own quant type
  + I64 id map), per-context ownership with a model-side weak-ref cache keyed
  by (N, buffer type), a BPE merge-order guard, and the graph hook in the
  qwen35 / qwen35moe / qwen4exp / gemma4-assistant MTP graphs.
- shared-NextN sidecars (nextn_shared_target_tensors, no output.weight) build
  the subset from the target's borrowed LM head via cparams.ctx_other.
- ggml-backend-meta: an arbitrary ROW RANGE of a 2-D tensor whose rows are
  split across devices (a vocabulary-split LM head) is spliced block by block.
  Without it `-sm tensor` aborted in the subset build (a 2-D axis-1 split
  could only be read whole, because its splice chunk is nb[axis + 1]).
- tests/test-mtp-draft-vocab.cpp (built, not ctest-registered: it needs a
  qwen35/qwen35moe model with an MTP head).

Gated on gfx1201 (2x R9700, ROCm 10.1.0), Qwen3.8-27B Q8_0, 2 GPU `-sm tensor`,
`draft-mtp-adaptive,ngram-mod --spec-draft-n-max 7 --spec-draft-mtp-vocab 98304`,
-n 3000 four-axis: R +1.3 %, P +1.7 %, C +2.4 %, K +0.8 % (+1.6 % aggregate)
against the same build with the flag off, with the `n_max <= 7` greedy-purity
promise verified with the trim on (three-way text identity vs `--spec-type
none` on prose and code).  MoE 35B-A3B is neutral.  gemma4 is wired up but not
beneficial on our payload (its useful cut is 245760 of 262144 rows, a no-op).
`test-backend-ops` 21179/21179, `test-logits-width-probe SPLIT=tensor` PASS
(W=1..8 maxdiff 0), prefill-logit KLD 0.000000 / 100.000 %.

